statement:
Let n, l be natural numbers, q a linear isometry of R^{n+l}, R a real number, and f : R^n -> R^l continuous on the closed ball B := B_R(0) of R^n (nothing is assumed off B). Write F(x) := q(graphPoint x (f x)). Write J_f(x) := sqrt(det(I_n + (<Df(x) e_a, Df(x) e_b>)_{a,b})), where:
- Df(x) = fderiv R f x, which is 0 where f is not differentiable;
- e_a = EuclideanSpace.single a 1;
- I_n is the identity matrix and + is entrywise matrix addition.
Then:
(i) for every Borel set A contained in B (MeasurableSet A for the Borel sigma-algebra of R^n = EuclideanSpace R (Fin n)), the image F(A) = q '' graphOver f A is a Borel subset of R^{n+l};
(ii) there is a Borel map Fh : R^n -> R^{n+l} with Fh(x) = F(x) for every x in B;
(iii) the function J_f : R^n -> R is Borel.
